    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. It follows the format of the earlier entries and uses the version and date from `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE`:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * CSV export for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads with backoff when the server returns 503 (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\nACME-421 (removing the `--legacy` flag from `sync`) is left out as you asked. It was the only change marked `!` in `merged_prs.txt`, which usually means a breaking change. With it reverted, nothing in this release breaks compatibility, so the minor version bump to 2.4.0 still fits. If the revert doesn't make it in before release, the flag removal will need to go back into the notes.",
